<article class="env-definition" id="8C3395">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8C3395">Definition <span data-tag="8C3395">4.3.3.2</span>.</a>Kan extension Let $\delta : K \rightarrow K'$ be a map of simplicial sets, and let $F: M^{op}(\delta ) \rightarrow \calD $ be a diagram in an $\infty $-category $\calD $ (which we view as a left extension of $f = F|K$ along $\delta $). We will say that $F$ is a <em>left Kan extension of $f$ along $\delta $</em> if there exists a commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { M^{op}(\delta ) \ar [r]^{F''} \ar [dr] &amp;  \calK \ar [r]^{F'} \ar [d]^{p} &amp;  \calD \\ &amp;  \Delta ^1 &amp;  } \]
</div>
  <p> where $F''$ is a categorical equivalence, $\calK $ is an $\infty $-category, $F= F' \circ F''$, and $F'$ is a left Kan extension of $F' | \calK \times _{ \Delta ^1} \{ 0\} $. </p>
</article>